safix::pass_locked

  × the entry 'alice/grafana' did not decrypt, so this mapping was not judged
  │ and
  │ nothing was written for it.
  │ 
  │ There is no safix option for this and there should not be: `pass` shells
  │ to
  │ gpg, and the unlock belongs to your own agent — it may answer from its
  │ cache, from a pinentry on a terminal this run does not have, or not at
  │ all.
  │ safix does not interpose on that, because interposing would defeat a
  │ hardware-backed key and would mean holding a passphrase safix has no use
  │ for.
  │ 
  │ This is not the absent-entry refusal: absence is answered from the store's
  │ own listing of names, so a backup mapping never writes over an entry it
  │ merely could not read.
  │ 
  │ gpg said:
  │ 
  │ gpg: decryption failed: No secret key
